# 100 approved drugs for a Boltz2 virtual screen against HIV-1 protease.
#
# SMILES <tab> name. Lines starting with # are ignored by the page.
#
# Canonical isomeric SMILES from PubChem (fetched by name), every one then
# parsed by this page own shared/chem/smiles.js - so each is a molecule the
# screen will actually accept, not merely valid SMILES.
#
# The first 9 are the approved HIV-1 PROTEASE INHIBITORS: they are what this
# target is clinically inhibited by, so a screen that works should rank them
# above the rest. The other 91 are approved drugs with unrelated targets.
#
# 🔴 THIS IS A SANITY CHECK, NOT A BENCHMARK. The decoys are not matched to
# the actives for molecular weight, logP or charge, so a ranking can separate
# them on size alone and look better than it is. Nine actives in a hundred is
# also too few for a confident enrichment number.
# 🔴 EVERY LINE IS ONE CONNECTED MOLECULE, WHICH IS NOT A STYLE RULE. The
# first version of this file had lithium carbonate -
# `[Li+].[Li+].C(=O)([O-])[O-]` - and the page refused it correctly:
# "this ligand is 3 disconnected fragments... Affinity is predicted for one
# molecule; split it, or remove the counter-ion." A salt or a co-crystal has
# no single binder to score. Replaced with chloroquine.
#
#
